# Shopping Mode (Epic E5)

> Branch: `jingduo-develop` ｜ Author: Jingduo Zhang (jzha0609)
> Scope: KitchMemo shopping cart feature (Epic E5 — Shopping Assistant & Smart Cart)

Brings household inventory into the shopping journey: review what's at home before buying, build a cart, warn about possible duplicate purchases, confirm and review at checkout, and turn completed purchases into inventory records.

---

## Feature overview (against the backlog)

| User Story | Feature | Status |
|---|---|---|
| US5.1 | Pre-Shop Review: read-only stock view with name / quantity / storage / expiry / **Use First** priority tag | ✅ |
| US5.2 | Build a cart: add (manual / photo), edit quantity, confirm (checkbox), delete | ✅ |
| US5.3 | Duplicate-purchase warning — expandable, lists every matching batch (quantity / storage / expiry) | ✅ |
| US5.4 | Checkout review of the confirmed (checked) cart, highlights duplicate warnings | ✅ |
| US5.5 | Confirmed items → editable inventory drafts, edit-and-confirm, leave prompt | ✅ |
| — | Photo recognition into the cart (reuses the team model, Plan A) | ✅ |

**Notes**: the recognition model itself is built by the team (recognises 8 fruit/veg + freshness); units are not localised (the stored string is shown as-is); "Use First" reuses the fridge's *expiring* threshold (not expired and ≤ 3 days left).

---

## Key flow (US5.2 → US5.5)

```
add to cart  →  check the box (confirm to buy)  →  Checkout review (confirmed only)
   →  add each to inventory (edit category/storage/expiry)  →  leave prompt if any unstocked
```

The checkbox is what makes an item a "confirmed" purchase: only checked items reach checkout, and the checkout button shows the confirmed count. This matches the "confirmed cart" wording in US5.4/US5.5.

